    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with a lineup anchored by **Junior Caminero** (70.80) and **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (64.80), our top-ranked plays. **Junior Caminero** benefits significantly from a favorable matchup against Sandy Alcantara; despite the park downgrade, the pitcher skill assessment and his placement in the #2 hole provide the highest floor in the lineup. Meanwhile, **Pete Crow-Armstrong** is an aggressive start despite the #8 slot; the optimizer is heavily weighting his elite sprint speed against Davis Martin, leveraging the Dynamic Platoon advantage to maximize stolen base potential in a category where we remain hyper-focused on efficiency.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the board was keeping **Hyeseong Kim** (49.35) on the bench. He trailed **Christian Yelich** (48.83) in the final model run, but the decision ultimately hinged on **Christian Yelich**\u2019s #3 lineup spot, which offsets his lower raw score. We are keeping a close watch on **Yordan Alvarez** (54.65); facing Jacob deGrom presents a significant risk, as his elite xwOBA is tempered by a negative -19% SP skill adjustment. Additionally, we remain cautious regarding the \"Lineup Pending\" status for much of the roster. If **Gary Sanchez** or **Kazuma Okamoto** are not confirmed in the #4 slot, their projected scores\u2014which rely on middle-order RBI opportunities\u2014will require an immediate re-evaluation to avoid falling below our 40-point efficiency floor. \n\nFinally, note the divergence in our outfield strategy. We are leaning on the aggression of **Luke Raley** (62.62), who earns a massive +19% boost from the matchup against Walker Buehler and the potential for stolen bases against a slow-delivery pitcher. Conversely, **Carson Benge** (55.60) represents a marginal play; while his leadoff spot is valuable, the negative platoon adjustment against Carlos Rod\u00f3n makes him a candidate to be swapped if defensive metrics shift closer to game time. We continue to hold **Zac Veen** and **Colt Keith** in reserve, as neither is currently available for activation to bolster our counting stats.",
